  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Who owns the compatible-capability lifecycle?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Decision 127: runtime.wasm owns the compatible-capability lifecycle on every host, including web. It owns instance ids, state validation, ordered lifecycle events, shutdown cleanup, Spec 1722 canonical start input, and the platforms[] allowlist. That behavior shipped in Traverse v0.17.1 (GitHub Release published 2026-11-16). Through v0.16.2, traverse_compatible_start/stop/kill returned -1 and web ran its own TypeScript lifecycle.',
